# verify-voice recall spam: stale observation index and a latchless alerter

Joel was paged every 30 minutes with "verify-voice FAILED: voice recall tool
registered with non-empty observation index" (2026-08-02, repeating for days).

## Root causes (three stacked)

1. **Stale observation index.** The recall tool wraps `joelclaw sessions
   search`, which reads the Typesense `observations` projection. Fresh
   observation pages existed in `dark-wizard/.brain/observations/` (72 files
   in 3 days) but the projection's newest doc was 2026-07-20 — the Observer
   loop stopped running its `joelclaw observations index` step ~07-21
   (its own self-reflection reports dispatcher-dedupe/telemetry state stale
   ~16,000+ minutes). Probe rightly returned NOTHING_DISTILLED for a 7-day
   window.
2. **Latchless alerter.** `verify-voice.sh` (launchd, every 30 min) fired
   `joelclaw notify send --priority urgent` AND `notification/call.requested`
   on EVERY failing tick — no state transition check.
3. **Gateway re-delivered repeats.** Stream receipts: 19 identical
   verify-voice failures in 24h → 15 delivery.requested. The one-incident-
   one-thread bar did not hold for this producer. Evidence for the gateway
   validation pass, not fixed here.

## Repair (verified live)

- Ran `joelclaw observations index`: 658 pages indexed; recall probe now
  returns real content (Reflector 07-30) and the full verify-voice suite
  passes 14/14.
- Added a transition latch to `verify-voice.sh`: alerts only when the failure
  set CHANGES; unchanged repeats are suppressed with a log line; recovery
  sends one normal-priority all-clear. State in
  `/tmp/joelclaw/verify-voice.failures` (reboot resets → one re-alert, fine).
- Installed `com.joelclaw.observations-index` LaunchAgent (hourly
  `joelclaw observations index`, RunAtLoad, Background/user-domain): recall
  freshness no longer depends on Observer loop health. First run exit 0.
- Reloaded the four observer LaunchAgents (tick/dream/herdr/neat-memory) —
  they were not loaded post-reboot; error 5 turned out to be
  "already bootstrapped" ambiguity, verified live in gui/501 afterward.

## Flagged for the Observer charter (not fixed here)

- Observer internals stale since ~07-21: dispatcher-dedupe, telemetry-state,
  pending-state, capture-outbox aging; `observer-context`/`observer-dream`
  logs missing; tick last exit code was 2 before this session. The loop
  writes pages but is not healthy. Owned by the observer charter in
  dark-wizard, needs its own session.
- Also skipped during indexing: a handful of `slack-work-state-pass` pages
  with invalid `sessionId` frontmatter — the producer writes pages the
  indexer rejects; worth a schema fix in that Inngest function.
